e Development – 101】\nL60:     * 【43†Biologics License Applications (BLAs) for CBER-Regulated Products】\nL61:     * 【44†Investigational New Drug Applications (INDs) for CBER-Regulated Products】\nL62:     * 【45†Device Submissions for CBER-Regulated Products】\nL63:     * 【46†Labeling for CBER-Regulated Products】\nL64:     * 【47†Master Files for CBER-Regulated Products】\nL65:     * 【48†New Drug Application (NDA) and Abbreviated New Drug Application (ANDA) for CBER-Regulated Products】\nL66:     * 【49†Formal Meetings and Requests for Feedback for CBER-Regulated Products】\nL67: # 2026 Biological License Application Approvals\nL68: \nL69: This list reflects information regarding the applications as of the approval date. It is not updated with regard to applicant or application status changes. The applications are listed by date of approval.\nL70: 2026 Biological License Application Approvals\nL71: Tradename/Proper Name       | Indication for Use  | STN  | Manufacturer/\nL72: License Number  | Approval Date\nL73: --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nL74: 【50†Fayuvi】rebisufligene etisparvovec-hopf  | Indicated for the treatment of neurologic manifestations of mucopolysaccharidosis type IIIA (MPS IIIA, Sanfilippo Syndrome type A) in pediatric patients with preserved neurodevelopmental function.  | 125845/0  | Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical Inc.5000 Marina Blvd.\nL75: Brisbane, CA 94005 Lic. # 2040  | 9/17/2026\nL76: \nL77: 【51†GENGLYCOS】pariglasgene brecaparvovec-opnr  | Indicated to reduce daily cornstarch intake as an adjunct to nutritional management in adult and pediatric patients 8 years of age and older with glycogen storage disease type Ia (GSDIa).  | 125858/0  | Ultragenyx Pharmaceutical, Inc.60 Leveroni Court\nL78: Novato, CA 94949 Lic. # 2390  | 8/19/2026\nL79: 【52†TUDRIQEV】vusolimogene oderparepvec-wtpg  | Indicated in combination with nivolumab for treatment of adult patients with unresectable advanced cutaneous melanoma who experienced disease progression with a programmed death receptor-1 (PD-1)-blocking antibody-based regimen.  | 125827/0  | Replimune, Inc.500 Unicorn Park Drive, Third Floor\nL80: Woburn, MA 01801 Lic. # 2360  | 8/6/2026\nL81: 【53†MFLUSIVA】Influenza Vaccine, mRNA       | Indicated for active immunization for the prevention of influenza disease caused by influenza virus subtypes A and type B represented in the vaccine in persons 50 years of age and older. The indication for persons 65 years of age and older is approved under accelerated approval pursuant to section 506(c) of the Federal Food, Drug, and Cosmetic Act (FDCA) and the regulations for accelerated approval, 21 CFR 601.41.  | 25869/0  | ModernaTX, Inc.325 Binney Street\nL82: Cambridge, MA 02142 Lic. # 2256  | 8/5/2026\nL83: 【54†EZPLAZ】Freeze Dried Plasma  | Indicated for transfusion in adults when plasma is required and other plasma products are not available. Indications include:\nL84: 1. Management of preoperative or bleeding patients who require replacement of multiple plasma coagulation factors [e.g., liver disease, disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC)].\nL85: 2. Patients undergoing massive transfusion who have clinically significant coagulation deficiencies.\nL86: 3. Patients taking warfarin who are bleeding or need to undergo an invasive procedure before vitamin K could reverse the warfarin effect or who need only transient reversal of warfarin effect.  | 125702/0  | Vascular Solutions, LLC (a subsidiary of Teleflex)\nL87: 6420 Sycamore Lane North\nL88: Maple Grove, MN 55369\nL89: Lic. # 2135  | 07/29/2026\nL90: Source Plasma  | Indicated for further manufacturing of injectable and injectable products.\nL91:    | 125870/0  | Care Plasma, LLC\nL92: ----------b6------------------b6-----------------\nL93: Lic. # 2407  | 07/27/2026\nL94: 【55†TREGZI】allogeneic regulatory T cell immunotherapy with HSPC and T cells-vldq\nL95:    | Indicated for use in matched donor hematopoietic stem cell transplantation with myeloablative preparative regimen,\nL96: for hematopoietic and immunologic reconstitution and to improve chronic graft-versushost disease (cGVHD)-free survival, in the treatment of adults with hematological\nL97: malignancies.  | 125868/0  | Orca Biosystems Inc.3475 Edison Way, Suite C\nL98: Menlo Park, CA 94025 Lic. # 2404  | 06/30/2026\nL99: 【56†OTARMENI】lunsotogene parvec-cwha\nL100:    | Indicated for the treatment of pediatric and adult patients with severe-to-profound and profound sensorineural hearing loss (any frequency >90 dB HL) associated with molecularly confirmed biallelic variants in the OTOF gene, preserved outer hair cell function, and no prior cochlear implant in the same ear.  | 125874/0  | Regeneron Pharmaceuticals, Inc.777 Old Saw Mill River Rd\nL101: Tarrytown, NY 10591 Lic. # 1760\nL102:    | 04/23/2026\nL103: 【57†KRESLADI】marnetegragene autotemcel  | Indicated for the treatment of pediatric patients with severe leukocyte adhesion deficiency-I (LAD-I) due to biallelic variants in ITGB2 without an available human leukocyte antigen (HLA)-matched sibling donor for allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplant.\nL104:    | 125806/0      | Rocket Pharmaceuticals, Inc.9 Cedarbrook Drive\nL105: Cranbury, NJ 08512 Lic. # 2328  | 03/26/2026\nL106: 【58†Procleix Plasmodium Assay】\nL107: Procleix Plasmodium Assay  | Intended for use in screening individual human donors, including donors of whole blood and blood components, and in screening living donors of organ and tissue samples when specimens are obtained while the donor’s heart is still beating. It is not intended for use on cord blood specimens. Whole blood donor samples are tested individually.  | 125862/0  | Grifols Diagnostic Solutions, Inc.\nL108: 10804 Willow Court San Diego, CA 92127\nL109: Lic. # 2032  | 03/16/2026\nL110: [Button: Feedback]\nL111: \nL112:   * 【59†FDA Archive】\nL113:   * 【21†About FDA】\nL114:   * 【60†Accessibility】\nL115: \nL116:   * 【61†Visitor Information】\nL117:   * 【62†Website Policies / Privacy】\nL118:   * 【63†No FEA